.TH TGDASH 1 "2026-02-11" "tgdash" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tgdash \- terminal dashboard for Terragrunt
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tgdash
.RB \-\- " command" " [args...]"
.br
.I command
.RB "2>&1 |"
.B tgdash
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tgdash
is a terminal dashboard that parses the prefixed output of
.BR "terragrunt run \-\-all"
and renders a real-time TUI showing per-unit status, plan summaries,
errors, and time estimates.
.PP
It supports two usage modes:
.TP
.B Exec mode
Run a command directly:
.BR "tgdash \-\- terragrunt run \-\-all plan" .
tgdash spawns the command and reads its output.
.TP
.B Pipe mode
Pipe output into tgdash:
.BR "terragrunt run \-\-all plan 2>&1 | tgdash" .
tgdash reads from standard input.
.PP
Any command that produces
.BI [ unit/path ]
prefixed output works with tgdash.
.PP
While the command is still running, each unit displays a status
indicator showing its current state.
A
.B \(bu running
label marks units that are currently executing.
When all units finish and the input stream closes, a
.B "Run complete."
message appears at the bottom of the screen.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.SS Navigation
.TS
l l.
j / Down	Move down
k / Up	Move up
gg	Jump to top
G	Jump to bottom
PgUp/PgDn	Scroll output
.TE
.SS Actions
.TS
l l.
Enter	Expand/collapse unit
Tab	Switch view
e	Toggle error filter
/	Search units by path
q / Ctrl+C	Quit
.TE
.PP
tgdash uses vim-style keybindings.
The
.B gg
binding requires pressing
.B g
twice in quick succession.
.SH VIEWS
.TP
.B Dashboard view
The default view.
Shows each unit with full detail including status, plan summary,
output lines, and timing information.
.TP
.B List view
A compact table showing all units at a glance.
Good for large repos with many units where you want to see overall
progress quickly.
Press
.B Tab
to switch between views.
.SH UNIT STATUS
Each unit displays one of the following status indicators:
.TS
l l.
\(ci wait	Waiting to start
\(bu running	Currently executing
\(OK done	Completed successfully
\(mu err	Completed with errors
\(es skip	Skipped
.TE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.tgdash/history.json
Run history used for time estimates.
tgdash records the duration of each unit after every run and uses
past data to estimate remaining time on subsequent runs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.TP
.B 1
Error starting the command (exec mode) or TUI error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a Terragrunt plan with the dashboard:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tgdash \-\- terragrunt run \-\-all plan
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pipe apply output into tgdash:
.PP
.RS
.nf
terragrunt run \-\-all apply 2>&1 | tgdash
.fi
.RE
.PP
Validate all units:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tgdash \-\- terragrunt run \-\-all validate
.fi
.RE
